    18	Where the work stands today exists **once**: `.planning/STATE.md`.
    19	
    20	## WHAT THIS HOLDING IS — read once; it does not change
    21	
    22	**DXB Global AI-Native Holding OS** — the executive command platform for one whole holding:
    23	companies, departments, directors, AI employees, projects, tasks, models, costs, decisions,
    24	approvals, workflows, skills, knowledge, memory, risks and audit, all seen, entered, changed and
    25	controlled from one place. It is **not** an admin panel, a project dashboard, an approval screen,
    26	a task manager or a SaaS panel — each is a named rejection in the CEO's own directive, and a
    27	delivery that resembles one is refused on sight.
    28	
    29	**Three faces, all three required:** it runs itself 7/24 (anti-baby-sitting) · the CEO sees every
    30	detail to the bottom · he changes anything at any moment, without having to micro-manage.
    31	
    32	**The standard is the Ferrari** (CEO, 2026-08-01): he ordered the car, not the drive — first place
    33	in a world competition, award standard, never amateur. Revenue and new companies come after; they
    34	are what the finished machine DOES.
    35	
    36	**The first law of V2 — IT MUST BE ALIVE** (*"CANSIZ DÜZ KİTAP GİBİ ORGANİZMA YOK SIFIR CANLILIK"*,
    37	2026-08-02). What the rival queue found, in one place:
    38	
    39	- The company is visibly working, and it keeps working when nobody is watching. A surface is
    40	  permanently attached to what the system is doing; it is not a page opened to find out.
    41	- You watch the work move: work travels between the workers on screen, the one who is working
    42	  lights up and is named, the idle one is still — **motion IS state**.
    43	- Movement means a real movement. A value moves until it is true and then stops; nothing loops for
    44	  decoration; rest is part of the design; **zero is a real answer**.
    45	- The surface follows the human: what is being talked about is what stands on the screen, put there
    46	  by the system and not by a click, within seconds.
    47	- The machine says when it last knew, and when it wakes next.
    48	- **His acceptance test:** he opens a screen, touches nothing, and within minutes something changes
    49	  because the company did work.
    50	
    51	Long form: `MASTER_PLAN.md` §1 · `HOLDING_OS_PRODUCT_SPEC.md` §§2-4 (his 19 control areas) ·
    52	`00-CEO-DIRECTIVE-BEKLENTILER.md`.
    53	
    54	## 0. YOUR FIRST REPLY IN A SESSION STATES THE POSITION
    55	
    56	Whatever he opens with — a greeting, a question, an order — **your first reply tells him where the
    57	work stands before anything else**, in four short lines in his language:
    58	
    59	1. what is finished and **waiting for his eye** (nothing is accepted until he looks — LAW B);
    60	2. what is **next**, and whether it waits on him or on you;
    61	3. what is **blocked on him** and cannot move without it;
    62	4. then answer what he actually said.
    63	
    64	**Empty is silent, not announced** (CEO order, 2026-09-22: *"gözünüzü bekleyen bir şey yok diye
    65	açılışta önüme gelmesin"*). Line 1 or line 3 is spoken only when it is true — something really is
    66	waiting for his eye, or really is blocked on him. When there is nothing there, that line is
    67	**dropped**, not replaced with "nothing is waiting" / "gözünüzü bekleyen bir şey yok". He reads
    68	four lines to find out what needs him; a line that exists only to say "nothing" costs him the read
    69	for zero content. This is scoped to this reply protocol only — it does not touch "zero is a real
    70	answer" above, which governs system state surfaces, not this greeting line.
    71	
    72	**The position is already in front of you** — the session-start hook carries where we left off,
    73	what is next and what waits on his approval; this file carries what the holding IS. **Never re-open a file
    74	to be told what you have already been told.** Measured 2026-08-10: a session re-read
