    78	
    79	## 1. AUTHORITY — when two sources disagree
    80	
    81	1. The CEO's order in this conversation
    82	2. His most recent written directive — `docs/ceo-directives/`
    83	3. The spec that owns the contract — `HOLDING-OS-MASTER-PLAN/`
    84	4. The open work board
    85	5. `.planning/STATE.md` — the current state photo
    86	6. Code, tests and schemas — evidence of what **is**, never of what **should be**
    87	7. Anything older, any summary, any memory
    88	
    89	**Never silently choose between conflicting sources.** Name the conflict, apply this order,
    90	say what you did.
    91	
    92	His live sentence beats every written rule beneath it. A written rule that pulls outside what he asked
    93	for is not obeyed — it is reported to him in one line, and he decides.
    94	
    95	**LAW A — a live CEO order DELETES what contradicts it** (CEO, 2026-07-30). Not a footnote
    96	beside it, not "superseded but retained". The contradicting text goes, and the report says
    97	what went. Keeping both is how a record starts lying.
